    "created_at": "2019-06-05T16:12:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-05T16:12:34Z",
    "body": "We have the similar comment in the spec: https://webaudio.github.io/web-audio-api/#priv-sec (see item 10)\r\n\r\nThe practical mitigation would be adding a low-pass filter to the browser's audio output, but Audio WG has decided not to do so because 1) it modifies the audio content in some ways and 2) the audio element currently does not have such mechanism. So even if WebAudio enforces a filter at its final output, it can be easily rerouted to an audio element.",
